  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 is the strongest evidence so far (avgpool 0.650, transformer 0.653), while image-only resnet50 is much weaker (single 0.208, multiprofile avgpool 0.328). The key uncertainty is whether adding image features can improve the strong RNA-only model. config_031 keeps the well-supported scvi_n200/multiprofile/avgpool settings and uses the already characterized resnet50 image encoder, so it mainly tests the effect of adding image plus fusion. Weighted fusion is a logical first multimodal test because the modalities are imbalanced; it can clarify whether adaptive fusion can exploit image signal without letting the weak image stream dominate. This is more informative than changing image encoder or aggregation simultaneously and has high expected value relative to the current RNA-only best."
}

